{
  "requirement": "`LanguageId` is a public struct with a private string. Construct one from `&str`\nor `String`, for example `LanguageId::from(\"rust\")`. `as_str()` borrows the\noriginal name. Serde represents the identifier as a string.\n\n`StructuralQuery::language` takes a `LanguageId`. Construction preserves the\nspelling. Structural search looks up the name among the configured languages\nand returns an error for an unknown name.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct LanguageId(/* private fields */);\n\nimpl LanguageId {\n    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for LanguageId;\nimpl Debug for LanguageId;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for LanguageId;\nimpl From<&str> for LanguageId;\nimpl From<String> for LanguageId;\nimpl Hash for LanguageId;\nimpl PartialEq for LanguageId;\nimpl Serialize for LanguageId;\nimpl Eq for LanguageId;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.sources.language_id`. Each obligation maps to a test as follows.\n\n- **Construction from `&str` and `String`, and `as_str()` returning the original name.** `source_bytes_error_kinds_and_language_names_round_trip` builds `LanguageId::from(\"CustomLang\")` and asserts `as_str() == \"CustomLang\"`. The mixed case checks that the spelling is preserved. It also asserts that `LanguageId::from(String::from(\"CustomLang\"))` equals the `&str`-built value. That covers both `From` impls and `PartialEq`/`Eq`.\n- **Serde as a string.** The same test asserts that `serde_json::to_value(&name)` equals the JSON string `\"CustomLang\"`. It also asserts that deserializing that value gives back an equal `LanguageId`.\n- **`StructuralQuery::language` takes a `LanguageId`, and construction preserves the spelling.** The same test builds `StructuralQuery::new(name, ..)` from a `LanguageId`. `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope` builds queries from `\"rust\".into()` and `\"python\".into()`. It asserts that the `rust` query finds only `.rs` matches and the `python` query finds only `script.py`. That shows a known name is looked up among the configured languages. It also reuses `query.language.clone()`, which exercises `Clone`.\n- **An error for an unknown name.** The first test asserts that `search_structure` on `CustomLang` returns `Err(SourceError::Invalid(message))` and that the message contains `CustomLang`.\n- **Trait implementations (`Clone`, `Debug`, `Deserialize`, `From<&str>`, `From<String>`, `Hash`, `PartialEq`, `Serialize`, `Eq`) and the public struct with a private field.** `public_exports_match_the_appendix` runs rustdoc and compares each documented declaration against the requirement text. Its `check_declaration` and `trait_impls` helpers compare the set of trait implementations for each item. That verifies the full impl list. The source shows the struct as `pub struct LanguageId(String)`, with `Clone`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Hash` and the serde traits derived. The `From` impls and `as_str` are trivial pass-throughs. No behavior of `Hash` or `Debug` beyond what the derives give is specified, so nothing further needs testing.\n\nI found no untested obligation and no counterexample the tests would accept. No acknowledgments (`{fixme}`) apply.",
